=== Stage 2: atomic swap on UTXO chains (eprint 2020/845 Fig. 1) ===

Master seed        : 6c61732d737761702f657072696e742d323032302d3834352f666967312f7631
Seed source        : pinned default
Swaps per config   : 10  (statistical floor 5)
Chains             : chain 1 (Bitcoin-like, 600 s blocks) <-> chain 2 (Litecoin-like, 150 s blocks)
LAS parameter setup: 956.572µs  (one-time, shared by configs 2 and 3)

Timing tier        : PACKED — every operation includes wire encode/decode.
                      Not comparable with Stage-1 core-tier numbers.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Configuration 1: Classical adaptor signature (ECDSA)
  signature : ECDSA adaptor signature (libsecp256k1-zkp)  [secp256k1, 256-bit group, ~128-bit classical security (no post-quantum security)]
  role-A pi : none required
              ECDSA adaptors have no knowledge gap: Ext recovers the discrete log exactly, so pre-signature adaptability is unconditional and Fig. 1's proof of witness knowledge is unnecessary. (The construction's own DLEQ proves pre-signature well-formedness by the pre-signer — a different claim — and is counted under the signature's communication cost, inside the pre-signature overhead.)
  binding   : e9bd349c4e73a797 (∃y : Y = y·G  (secp256k1 discrete log))
  fully PQ  : no

  Execution time, per protocol phase (mean +/- sample SD over 10 swaps):
    KeyGen x2 + Gen                58.4 +/-       9.7 us
    PreSign (u1, tx1)             114.9 +/-      18.4 us
    PreVerify (u2 gate)           147.6 +/-      35.1 us
    PreSign (u2, tx2)             107.1 +/-      14.5 us
    Adapt (u1 -> sigma2)          138.4 +/-      16.4 us
    Settle chain 2                 51.9 +/-      16.7 us
    Ext (u2)                       25.3 +/-       4.5 us
    Adapt (u2 -> sigma1)          132.7 +/-      19.3 us
    Settle chain 1                 43.4 +/-       7.8 us
    end-to-end                    819.7 +/-      93.1 us   (context only, not the headline)
    one-time setup         signature 38.502µs, proof n/a
      (setup is excluded from every phase above)

  Communication cost, per message (observed over 10 swaps, identical in every run):
    Y (statement)                    33 B   u1 -> u2 (off-chain)
    sigma_hat_1                     162 B   u1 -> u2 (off-chain)
    tx1                             114 B   u1 -> u2 (off-chain)
    sigma_hat_2                     162 B   u2 -> u1 (off-chain)
    tx2                             114 B   u2 -> u1 (off-chain)
    tx2 + sigma_2                   178 B   published on chain 2
    tx1 + sigma_1                   178 B   published on chain 1
    ---------------------- --------------
    subtotal                        585 B   off-chain
    subtotal                        356 B   on-chain
    TOTAL                           941 B   per swap

  Object sizes (fixed per scheme, reported once):
    public key       33 B   secret key       32 B
    statement        33 B   witness          32 B
    signature        64 B   pre-signature   162 B  (overhead 98 B)

